#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405628 :multistep/context "Source question: 4.\n\nConsider $x(t)=5\\sin t$ and $y(t)=5\\cos t$, where $0\\le t\\le2\\pi$. Use exact values." :multistep/id #uuid "85dfec84-a988-56e8-b658-a46ba3bdd809" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405379 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405976}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405641 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405655}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405631 :multistep/context "Source question: 5.\n\n**Implicit differentiation — multivariable**\n\nLet $f(x,y,z)$ be a scalar function and consider the level surface $f(x,y,z)=c$. Regard $z$ as a function of independent variables $x$ and $y$, so $\\partial y/\\partial x=\\partial x/\\partial y=0$. The dependence tree is:\n\n![f depends on x, y, and z; each branch is differentiated with respect to x and y](images/e6/e62ca88ac96b7eff736b8f6e72079a49562861ebcec69b3be4150e5efe087c90.png)" :multistep/id #uuid "862cc95f-2d16-59de-83e5-3c4048895e63" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405260 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405507}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405489 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405337}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405495 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405245}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405638 :multistep/context "Source question: 4(a)–(b), PDF page 5.\n\n**Unit vectors in polar coordinates.** Consider $P(x,y)$, $$\n\\displaystyle \\mathbf r=\\overrightarrow{OP}=\\langle x,y\\rangle=\\langle r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta\\rangle,\n$$ the unit circle centered at P, and\n\n$$\\mathbf i=\\langle1,0\\rangle,\\quad\\mathbf j=\\langle0,1\\rangle,\\quad\\hat{\\mathbf r}=\\langle\\cos\\theta,\\sin\\theta\\rangle,\\quad\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}=\\langle-\\sin\\theta,\\cos\\theta\\rangle.$$\n\n![Source polar unit vectors at P](images/35/35a19c56fb5bee3177ff22b713fb8f5b30ea312559b5a1024abcc8360deb2b9e.png)" :multistep/id #uuid "880e33b4-548c-5f00-a2dc-f3f54b6cc045" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405610 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405689}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405706 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405362}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405651 :multistep/context "Source question: 11(a)–(b)." :multistep/id #uuid "8be4e529-b068-50b1-9fb5-96f48c8389d2" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405274 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405428}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405516 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405687}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405666 :multistep/context "Source question: 5(a)–(d), PDF page 6.\n\nUse Problem 4(b) to express each field entirely in $r,\\theta,\\hat{\\mathbf r},\\hat{\\boldsymbol\\theta}$. Treat the unit vectors as directions of increasing r and θ and reflect on whether the results make sense in the field plots." :multistep/id #uuid "90720a6d-ddb7-5303-9b25-3a4c14c8c708" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405211 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405774}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405243 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405829}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405554 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405342}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405804 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405522}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405669 :multistep/context "Source question: 4.\n\nFor $x(t)=t^3-144t$ and $y(t)=2t^2$, find all points with horizontal or vertical tangent lines. Give exact coordinate pairs as a comma-separated list; enter `DNE` if there are none." :multistep/id #uuid "91143f11-89c8-563a-afa3-9a3d2e8b071c" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405574 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405425}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405867 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405837}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405683 :multistep/context "Source question: 2.\n\nSolving initial value problems was an important application of integration from MTH 252. Recall that the function $y(x)$ satisfying\n\n$$\ny'(x)=f(x),\\qquad y(x_0)=a\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\ny(x)=a+\\int_{x_0}^x f(s)\\,ds.\n$$\n\nThe function $y(x)$ is known as the solution to the initial value problem. Solve the following initial value problems:" :multistep/id #uuid "9768ff19-fbdb-57cb-98b2-c90310055446" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405715 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405952}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405846 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405670}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405936 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405711}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405953 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405511}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405688 :multistep/context "Source question: 1.\n\n**Area of a parallelogram**\n\nConsider the parallelogram formed by $\\mathbf u$ and $\\mathbf v$. Let $\\theta$ be the angle between them.\n\n![Parallelogram formed by u and v with included angle theta](images/ca/ca9c54ad7c41bea1e72278f7d24742fbde8a4f6a4abf46b7ddadf557dad7bae4.png)" :multistep/id #uuid "99c3ae3a-448c-526b-96b7-0c561f1a8187" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405366 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405691}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405382 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405572}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405404 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405712}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405707 :multistep/context "Source question: 9.\n\nConsider the spiral $x(t)=t\\cos t$, $y(t)=t\\sin t$, for $0\\le t\\le5\\pi$." :multistep/id #uuid "9f56feff-ea76-5578-9e9e-96bddae8fa6a" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405656 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405469}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405794 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405261}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405717 :multistep/context "Source question: 6.\n\n**The 3D gradient is orthogonal to a level surface**\n\nLet $\\varphi(x,y,z)$ be a scalar function with level surface $\\varphi(x,y,z)=c$. From Problem 5, $$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}=-\\dfrac{\\varphi_x}{\\varphi_z}\n$$ and $$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}=-\\dfrac{\\varphi_y}{\\varphi_z}.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "a275c6a2-50ca-57bf-9cae-18b542d4439e" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405673 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405472}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405817 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405662}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405992 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405374}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405724 :multistep/context "Source question: 2(a)–(c), PDF page 3.\n\nLet $\\mathbf F(x,y)=\\mathbf r/|\\mathbf r|=\\langle x,y\\rangle/\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}$, $\\eta(x,y)=x^2+y^2$, and $C: x^2+y^2=a^2$, with $a>0$." :multistep/id #uuid "a5643d60-a09c-5b5b-995a-c6199fd64e65" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405288 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405823}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405603 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405805}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405654 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405825}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405725 :multistep/context "Source question: 6.\n\nConsider $x(t)=2\\sin t-3$ and $y(t)=2\\cos t+1$, with $0\\le t\\le\\pi$. Use exact values." :multistep/id #uuid "a58eb7e9-eb11-5616-9332-9ba68bbd43cc" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405619 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405349}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405955 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405304}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405738 :multistep/context "[Open in WeBWorK](https://webwork2.science.oregonstate.edu/webwork2/MTH_256_020_F2026/WebWork_1/4)\n\nIn this problem you will solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\nxy'=9y-6x,\\qquad y(1)=-4.\n$$" :multistep/id #uuid "abcf5322-e31b-58c5-acc9-c0a106bdc0b3" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405564 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405583}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405685 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405326}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405930 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405581}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405739 :multistep/context "Source question: 3.\n\nThe direction field for\n\n$$\ny'=\\frac{x}{y}\n$$\n\nis provided below. On the direction field sketch and label the following:\n\n![Direction field for y prime equals x over y](images/2a/2ab36389693808aef75de9ab5f665a9956c672a1a6f12c850a380991b08abbd8.png)" :multistep/id #uuid "ac83bc65-e101-5c37-ab8f-09ba2fd53da9" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405458 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405785}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405635 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405534}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405888 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405332}}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405755 :multistep/context "Source question: 12(a)–(c).\n\nFind $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_C e^x\\cos y\\,dx-e^x\\sin y\\,dy\n$$ for each curve C." :multistep/id #uuid "b2d2c0fa-8ad3-5edf-9d0d-eb348fd31800" :multistep/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405384 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405476}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405413 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405383}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405789 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186405335}}]}]}
